# deploy.manifest — the DECLARED, AUDITABLE asset closure for the rpi5 carousel
# kiosk.  This file is the single source of truth for "what deploys".  Each
# non-comment line is a path relative to the repo root (…/composeio); a trailing
# slash means a directory (synced recursively).  `deploy_rpi5.sh` reads this and
# rsyncs each entry (preserving path structure) to
# davidleeburnett@pi.example.local:~/maker/composeio/.
#
# WHY A MANIFEST: the kiosk once shipped the python package but NOT the
# compose_projects/ authoring tree, so the CIC nav (cic_menu_structure.md) was
# missing and both consoles' tab rows blanked (defect 2026-07-31).  A file-copy
# deploy that isn't declared drifts silently.  This manifest makes the closure
# reviewable: if a running scene references an asset, it MUST be listed here.
#
# ── THE VERIFIED RUNTIME CLOSURE (what the carousel kiosk actually loads) ──
# kiosk.py spawns `run_compose <scene> --fullscreen --transports` (cwd = repo
# root) for two scenes, both under compose_projects/carousel/:
#   • launcher.compose.yaml → tile icons are BUS ASSETS
#       (bus://assets/icons/carousel/{fiat_logo,bsg_shield,power_off}.png) the
#       render engine resolves BY REFERENCE from the store at draw time — NOT
#       file-copied here (2026-08-04; scripts/publish_carousel_assets.py).
#   • bsg_app.compose.yaml   → the colonial_console 2-up.  It declares
#       `widget_modules: [compose_projects.bsg.widgets]`, so the kiosk imports
#       the PROJECT-LOCAL BSG widget cluster ([CXC-PROJECT-WIDGETS]) — that
#       subtree (+ its package-init chain) MUST ship or the import fails and both
#       consoles render placeholders.  The CIC chrome / EXT view / nav are BUS
#       ASSETS (bus://assets/cic/…) resolved BY REFERENCE from the store.
# Fonts load from fonts/ (COMPOSEIO_FONT_DIR).
#
# ── CIC ART IS NOT DEPLOYED — THE STORE SERVES IT (2026-08-04) ──
# The colonial_console chrome/EXT/nav are published to the bus asset store
# (scripts/publish_cic_assets.py → bus://assets/cic/{chrome,ext}.svg + menu.md +
# icons/cic/planet.jpg) and resolved by reference (svg_art.CHROME_URI/EXT_URI,
# menu.MENU_URI).  This retires the prior file-copy of cic_menu_structure.md.
# The package's bundled OFFLINE-fallback copies now live WITH the project-local
# widget cluster — compose_projects/bsg/widgets/cic/{colonial_console_chrome.svg,
# colonial_console_ext.svg,cic_menu_default.md} — so a store-unreachable kiosk
# still draws the frame + tab rows (never blank).  ([CXC-PROJECT-WIDGETS] moved
# this cluster out of python/ where the deploy used to pick it up; hence the
# explicit widgets entries below.)

# The render engine + generic widgets.
python/

# The two kiosk scenes, kiosk.py supervisor, and this tooling.  The tile icon
# PNGs under carousel/resources/ are AUTHORING sources served from the store —
# excluded from the sync in deploy_rpi5.sh (RSYNC_EXCLUDES).
compose_projects/carousel/

# The PROJECT-LOCAL BSG widget cluster ([CXC-PROJECT-WIDGETS]) the 2-up scene
# imports via `widget_modules:` — the colonial_console shell, cic_tab_row, and
# the CIC bundled OFFLINE-fallback art (widgets/cic/).  MUST ship WITH its
# package-init chain so `import compose_projects.bsg.widgets` resolves: rsync -R
# ships only files UNDER a listed dir, so the parent __init__.py markers are
# listed explicitly (they are safe/lazy — bsg/__init__.py defers BSGApp so no CTk
# import is dragged onto the headless kiosk).
compose_projects/__init__.py
compose_projects/bsg/__init__.py
compose_projects/bsg/widgets/

# The CIC composition-model surfaces the compositing slice reads DIRECTLY at
# runtime ([SPEC:CXC-COMP]; colonial_console.py -> cic/composite.py resource_svg):
# colonial_base_ux.svg + <mode>_mode.svg are the SINGLE SOURCE now (superseding the
# bus-baked-chrome / EXT-only model — the runtime reads these local files). ~960K,
# all small; ships the whole dir so David's evolving mode SVGs + cic_assets.yaml
# ride along. The EXT rotation IMAGES stay bus-resolved (bus://assets/cic/screens/).
compose_projects/bsg/resources/screen_base_layout/

# The engine-thrust panel SCENE ([DD-MENU-SLOT-SCENE-GRAMMAR] Arm A) —
# std-helm-heading.svg's `slot:scene@engine-thrust` mounts this
# `.compose.yaml` BY REFERENCE at colonial_console build time
# (cic/composite.py mount_scene() -> SCENE_FIXTURES -> parse_compose_yaml),
# so it is now a RUNTIME dependency of the 2-up, not just device-config for a
# separate service.  Scoped to the ONE sub-directory the mount path reads —
# NOT the whole game_hardware/ tree (still omitted below).
compose_projects/bsg/game_hardware/__init__.py
compose_projects/bsg/game_hardware/engine_thrust_panel/

# Typography (COMPOSEIO_FONT_DIR).
fonts/

# ── DELIBERATELY OMITTED (not referenced by the carousel kiosk scenes) ──
# Listed here so the omission is a decision, not an oversight.  If a future
# kiosk scene references any of these, ADD it above (that is the whole point of
# the manifest) — do not deploy out-of-band.
#   compose_projects/carousel/resources/*.png      the launcher tile icons —
#       AUTHORING sources, PUBLISHED to bus://assets/icons/carousel/… and
#       resolved by reference; the kiosk is always store-reachable, so they are
#       excluded from the sync (deploy_rpi5.sh RSYNC_EXCLUDES).  The generic
#       image widget has no bundled-fallback slot (only a placeholder swatch),
#       so none is shipped — re-publish with scripts/publish_carousel_assets.py.
#   compose_projects/bsg/{world,engine,client}/ + most of game_hardware/ + most
#       of resources/ stay omitted (game code/content) — but bsg/widgets/ + the
#       two parent __init__.py markers now SHIP (listed above): the 2-up imports
#       the project-local widget cluster.
#   compose_projects/bsg/resources/sfx/            47M mp3 — game audio, no kiosk scene uses it
#   compose_projects/bsg/resources/screens/        game backdrops — not in the 2-up
#   compose_projects/bsg/world|engine|client/  game sim code — runs elsewhere
#   compose_projects/bsg/game_hardware/  device configs for separate services —
#       EXCEPT engine_thrust_panel/ (now SHIPS, listed in the active section
#       above): std-helm-heading.svg's `slot:scene@engine-thrust` drop-in reads
#       engine_thrust.compose.yaml directly at colonial_console build time, so
#       it is a runtime dependency of the 2-up now, unlike every other
#       game_hardware/ device config.
#   compose_projects/bsg/resources/{characters,locations,ships,missions}/  game content
#   (screen_base_layout/ now SHIPS — listed in the active section above.  Superseded
#       2026-08-05 by the compositing slice [SPEC:CXC-COMP]: colonial_console.py reads
#       the authoring base+mode SVGs DIRECTLY at runtime via cic/composite.py, so the
#       kiosk must carry them.  The old "chrome baked into the package + ext resolved
#       from the bus, screen_base_layout never read locally" model is retired.  The
#       chrome/ext bus assets + the rotation images [bus://assets/cic/screens/*.jpg]
#       stay bus-resolved — the local SVGs are the composition source, the bus serves
#       the referenced raster assets.)
